  "result": "## Summary\n\nCustomer statements have been successfully implemented. Here's what was added:\n\n**New file: `src/statements.js`**\n- `statement(customerId, invoices, asOf)` function that:\n  - Validates the customer exists (returns `CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND` if not)\n  - Filters invoices to only those with:\n    - Matching customerId\n    - Status 'issued' or 'partially_paid'\n    - issueDate on or before asOf\n  - Returns `ok({ customerId, invoices, totalDue })`\n  - Each invoice in the array includes: `{ number, issueDate, dueDate, total, due }`\n  - Invoices sorted by issueDate (ascending)\n  - totalDue is the sum of all due amounts\n  - Properly calculates totals using invoiceTotals (including discounts, VAT, and vouchers)\n  - Does not mutate the input invoices array\n\n**New test file: `test/statements.test.js`**\n- 17 comprehensive tests covering:\n  - Empty statement for customer with no invoices\n  - Unknown customer error handling\n  - Filtering by status (issued, partially_paid, excluding draft/paid)\n  - Date filtering (asOf cutoff)\n  - Sorting by issueDate\n  - Total and totalDue calculations\n  - Partial payment handling\n  - Multi-customer filtering\n  - Mixed invoice statuses\n  - Voucher support\n  - Immutability of input\n\nAll 199 tests pass (182 previous + 17 new). The statement function properly aggregates customer invoices with their outstanding amounts, providing a complete view of what's due.",
